  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Tokenized stocks printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $2.55B (+0.4% 30D) keeps the lane in a holding pattern\u2014liquidity and platform concentration still dominate. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tokens/money-mushroom-moved-a-nasdaq-penny-stock-but-its-tokenized-stock-is-a-memecoin-too\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">&#x27;Money Mushroom&#x27; Moved A Nasdaq Penny Stock, But Its &#x27;Tokenized Stock&#x27; Is A Memecoin Too</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Tokenized stocks remain an early-stage lane:</strong> liquidity and scale are still concentrated in a small set of platforms/networks. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/converge/tradfi-and-fintech/bitwise-launches-self-custodied-tokenized-stock-portfolio-on-base\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bitwise Launches Self-Custodied Tokenized Stock Portfolio on Base</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Tokenized equities remain an early access market:</strong> Liquidity and scale stay concentrated until broker distribution and custody plumbing can support broader trading. Related: <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxOSXdJcnJpLU1Fc0s2alBlNm8wV1p6ZFJVZE40cUgwVkVDSDAxRDRHLV9kemlSWTc4UHFLcnZ1YW02cl9OdHM1MEdKQTZDczM1VWZlUFFleGpKaWMyc3JoU2N0YUtnUU1zdzkzWS15c3lGRC1PWWtMZmRZQ2IzNTVfQ192b1dFSHpCcHF3aDZoQ01Mckt3Z2pWakFoaHU2TzBnRWZkdW5obU5rQ0Q1cEREd1ZDSnM5b2prUnUxdA?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Coinbase tokenized stocks hit $100M in volume; first Zcash ETF and Strategy yield goes DeFi</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Securities and broker-rule constraints often set the pace more than listing count, so near-term share stays tied to venues that can actually distribute products. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/09/01/sec-proposes-transfer-agent-rule-sets-event-to-figure-out-round-the-clock-u-s-trading\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SEC proposes transfer agent rule, sets event to figure out round-the-clock U.S. trading</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
